@startuml sequence-oauth
!include theme.iuml
title Trilium ETAPI MCP — OAuth 2.1 flow

skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
autonumber

actor "User\n(browser)" as User
participant "MCP client\n(app)" as Client

box "trilium-mcp (this repo)"
    participant "TriliumOAuthProvider\n(/register /authorize\n/login /token /revoke)" as AS #F4C48D
    participant "FastMCP\n+ EtapiTokenAuth" as MCP #98D486
    database "mcp-oauth\n(encrypted)" as Store
end box

participant "Trilium\nETAPI" as Trilium

== Discovery and registration ==
Client -> MCP : POST /mcp (no token)
MCP --> Client : 401\nWWW-Authenticate: Bearer resource_metadata=…
Client -> AS : GET /.well-known/…\nPOST /register
AS -> Store : save client
AS --> Client : client_id

== Login (once per client) ==
Client -> AS : GET /authorize (PKCE)
AS -> Store : pending login
AS --> User : redirect to /login
User -> AS : POST /login\nTrilium password
AS -> Trilium : POST /auth/login {password}
Trilium --> AS : new ETAPI token
note right of AS : Password is used once,\nnever stored or logged.
AS -> Store : auth code → ETAPI token
AS --> Client : redirect with code
Client -> AS : POST /token (code + verifier)
AS -> Store : tmcp_ access + refresh token\n→ ETAPI token
AS --> Client : access token (1 h)\nrefresh token (30 d)

== Tool call ==
Client -> MCP : POST /mcp\nAuthorization: Bearer <access token>
MCP -> AS : verify_token
AS -> Store : look up
AS --> MCP : claims.etapi_token
MCP -> Trilium : /etapi/…\nAuthorization: <ETAPI token>
Trilium --> MCP : JSON
MCP --> Client : tool result

== Refresh and revoke ==
Client -> AS : POST /token (refresh_token)
AS -> Store : rotate pair, same ETAPI token
AS --> Client : new access + refresh token
Client -> AS : POST /revoke
AS -> Store : drop pair
AS -> Trilium : POST /auth/logout\n(deletes the minted ETAPI token)

@enduml
